# naudio 3

https://www.reddit.com/r/dotnet/comments/1n0lf5s/microsoftwindowssdknetdll_doubling_the_size_of/
A common complaint on developer forums like Reddit's .NET Community is that Microsoft.Windows.SDK.NET.dll can significantly bloat application size (often adding 20MB to 40MB or more to the build output). This occurs because it contains the C# definitions for every available WinRT API in the OS.The Fix: To minimize this overhead, ensure that IL Trimming (<PublishTrimmed>true</PublishTrimmed>) is enabled in your .csproj file when publishing your application. Trimming strips out the unused WinRT mappings, reducing the final footprint of the DLL to only what your application actually calls.

